Subject: [PATCH 002/230] Harden auth: timing-safe initData compare, required
 auth_date, prod dev-secret boot guard
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- verifyInitData: constant-time digest compare; auth_date now required and
  freshness-enforced (a leaked initData is no longer an immortal credential)
- TEMP auth probe on /api/auth/guest: logs verify verdict + identity mode
  (telegram vs guest), no secrets — watching whether real Telegram clients
  fail verification; signature handling deliberately unchanged
- server refuses to boot when NODE_ENV=production and DEV_AUTH_SECRET is set
- writeLimiter added to ratings and comments POSTs
- trust proxy pinned to 1 hop instead of trusting any chain
- new tests/verify.test.ts pins the verification contract

